.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KEM-ML-KEM 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KEM-ML-KEM-512 ,
.Nm EVP_KEM-ML-KEM-768 ,
.Nm EVP_KEM-ML-KEM-1024 ,
.Nm EVP_KEM-ML-KEM
.Nd EVP_KEM ML-KEM keytype and algorithm support
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Sy ML-KEM
keytypes and parameters are described in
.Xr EVP_PKEY-ML-KEM 7 .
See
.Xr EVP_PKEY_encapsulate 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_decapsulate 3
for more details about basic KEM operations.
.Ss ML-KEM KEM parameters
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqikme" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KEM_PARAM_IKME Ns ) <octet string>
The OpenSSL ML-KEM encapsulation mechanism can only be modified by
setting randomness during encapsulation, this enables testing, as per
FIPS 203, section 6.2, algorithm 17.
.Pp
This parameter should not be used for purposes other than testing.
.Pp
When this parameter is not set, encapsulation proceeds as per FIPS 203,
section 7.2
.Pp
This parameter is only settable.
.El
.Pp
This can be set when using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_encapsulate_init 3 .
.Sh CONFORMING TO
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It FIPS203
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_encapsulate 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_decapsulate 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KEYMGMT 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY 3 ,
.Xr provider-keymgmt 7
.Sh HISTORY
This functionality was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
